        "answer": {
          "short": "$(1,4)$",
          "worked": "Substitute $y=2x+2$ into $y=x^2+3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+2&=x^2+3\\\\x^2-2x+1&=0\\\\(x-1)^2&=0\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $x=1$ into $y=2x+2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2(1)+2\\\\y&=4\\end{align*}$$\nThe solution is $(1,4)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
