        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-2.5,45)$",
          "worked": "Substitute $y=-20x-5$ into $y=4x^2+20$.\n$$\\begin{align*}-20x-5&=4x^2+20\\\\4x^2+20x+25&=0\\\\(2x+5)^2&=0\\\\2x+5&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac{5}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $x=-\\frac{5}{2}$ into $y=-20x-5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-20\\left(-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)-5\\\\y&=45\\end{align*}$$\nThe solution is $\\left(-\\frac{5}{2},45\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
